# CODEOWNERS · copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace the handles.
# Rules: teams, not individuals (people leave; teams get reassigned on a handover). No path without an owner: the
# catch-all line comes first, and later lines override it. Turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch
# protection or rulesets, or this file is documentation only.
# Manual chapter 18 §c (Agentic Coding Swarm Protocol).

# Everything: the team that owns the project.
*                               @your-org/project-team

# The gates. Weakening any of them needs the playbook owner as well (MAINTAINING.md in the protocol repo).
/swarm.json                     @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
/scripts/dev/                   @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
**/architecture.test.*          @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
**/docs.test.*                  @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
**/vitest.config.*              @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
/.claude/settings.json          @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
/quality-ratchets.json          @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
/CLAUDE.md                      @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners
/AGENTS.md                      @your-org/project-team @your-org/playbook-owners

# Operations and handover: whoever runs production signs off.
/docs/runbook.md                @your-org/project-team @your-org/ops
/docs/dependencies.md           @your-org/project-team @your-org/ops
/docs/handover/                 @your-org/project-team
/.env.example                   @your-org/project-team @your-org/ops

# Decisions.
/docs/adr/                      @your-org/project-team

# Areas owned by another team (examples).
# /src/billing/                 @your-org/payments
# /infra/                       @your-org/platform
